From: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] evaluate scalar map lookups as left binary operands

Allow a parenthesized map on the left of a binary expression and explicitly
parenthesized runtime selectors on its right. Keep keyword RHS values distinct
from packet selectors, preserving flag masks and statement boundaries without
parser conflicts. Restrict JSON input to the same text save/load contract.
Normalize scalar map result metadata at the binary-operand boundary, keeping
legacy map statement validation unchanged. Restore scalar metadata when reading
lookup registers, and give JSON child operands their own grammar contexts.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
